dot/pull/102158#issuecomment-2623141510","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102158","id":2623141510,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cWfaG","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-29T23:17:59Z","updated_at":"2025-01-29T23:17:59Z","body":"Out of curiosity, is there a reason to prefer a different fallback order than what's being done now? We need to make sure the added complexity to the fallback is worth it. I suggest opening a [proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals) for this.\r\n\r\nI'd imagine you always want to fallback to either D3D12 or Metal when Vulkan isn't supported, or vice versa, so that you remain on a RenderingDevice-based rendering method whenever possible (only falling back to Compatibility when there is no alternative).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2623141510/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.githu